# Curriculum freshness rules

- Every mechanism claim in `steps/**` carries a `[n]` marker resolving to
  `bibliography.md` per `specs/citation-format.md`; third-party claims add
  `[third-party]`.
- Every claim traces to a source URL that was fetched and content-verified
  with an access date no older than a rolling 14 days from the last
  successful content verification. A reachable URL or HTTP 200 alone does
  not count as verification; body text must have been inspected.
- New or changed claims get a `fact-check.md` row (claim/source/date/
  verdict) per `specs/fact-check-schema.md`; only `confirmed`, `corrected`,
  or `cut` are valid verdicts.
- Re-runs of a refresh must not duplicate bibliography entries: match on URL
  before adding, and update existing entries in place.
- Findings about features absent from the audited curriculum are recorded as
  "new to coverage"; never as "newly shipped" without fetched release
  evidence.
- A failed URL fetch is recorded as unavailable, not deprecated; it blocks
  only the dependent work and is documented with its blocker.
- Freshness findings are classified (critical correction / deepen / new
  optional / footnote / defer) with stable IDs and a change ledger so an
  interrupted refresh can resume without losing pending items.
- Applying changes from a refresh requires user approval after findings are
  reported; changed step files are marked `needs-review` without erasing
  learner progress; case-study edits are additive-only except documented
  freshness invalidation. No publish, deploy, or push during a refresh.
